# {{ .Binary }}

A commerce server built on [gobit]({{ .GobitModule }}).

## Run it

```
go mod tidy                   # resolve the library's own dependencies, once
docker compose up -d          # Postgres and Redis
# fill in JWT_SECRET, ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL and ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD in .env
go run .                      # the server starts when there are NO arguments
```

The schema is applied AT STARTUP by every module that owns one, so there is no
migrate-up step to forget. `go run . help` lists the operator subcommands.

## What is in here

`main.go` is the whole program: it chooses which modules and plugins are
installed and hands the rest to `gobit.App`. Add your own module with `.Add()`
and a plugin with `.Use()`.
{{ if .Replace }}
## Before you share this

`go.mod` carries a `replace` line pointing at a gobit checkout on the machine
that generated this project. Remove it and require a released version instead,
or nobody else can build this.
{{ end }}
